==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈsædl̩/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-saddle.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ædəl|lang=en}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|sadel}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|sadol}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*sadulaz}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*sod-tlō-}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*sed-||to sit}}. Cognate with Scots {{m|sco|sadil}}, Saterland Frisian {{m|stq|Soadel}}, West Frisian {{m|fy|seal}}, Dutch {{m|nl|zadel}}, Low German {{m|nds|Sadel}}, German {{m|de|Sattel}}, Danish {{m|da|sadel}}, Russian {{m|ru|седло́}}, Swedish {{m|sv|sadel}}, Icelandic {{m|is|söðull}}.

====Noun====
[[Image:StubbenTristan.jpg|thumb|An "English" style saddle used for riding horses.]]
{{en-noun}}

# A [[seat]] ([[tack]]) for a [[rider]] placed on the back of a [[horse]] or other [[animal]]
# An item of [[harness]] (harness saddle) placed on the back of a horse or other animal
# A seat on a [[bicycle]], [[motorcycle]] etc
# A [[cut]] of [[meat]] that includes both [[loin]]s and part of the [[backbone]]
# A low point, in the shape of a saddle, between two [[hills]].
#* '''1977''', {{w|John Le Carré}}, ''The Honourable Schoolboy'', Folio Society 2010, p. 483:
#*: With Lizzie leading, they scrambled quickly over several false peaks towards the '''saddle'''.
# {{lb|en|mining}} A [[formation]] of [[gold]]-bearing [[quartz]] occurring along the crest of an [[anticlinal]] [[fold]], especially in [[Australia]].
# The raised floorboard in a [[doorway]].
# {{label|en|construction}} A small tapered/sloped area structure that helps channel surface water to drains.
# {{label|en|nautical}} A block of wood, usually fastened to one [[spar]] and shaped to receive the end of another.
# {{label|en|engineering}} A part, such as a [[flange]], which is hollowed out to fit upon a convex surface and serve as a means of attachment or support.
# The [[clitellus]] of an [[earthworm]].

